{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XGWL1CpAX32d5WeWp6f896","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-508\"\n3\ttitle = \"The architectural remapping program: blind minimal-map re-derivation, divergences filed as consolidation WIs\"\n4\tspecref = \"docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-58\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = [\"SR-163\"]\n7\tneeds = [\"WI-448\", \"WI-483\", \"WI-507\"]\n8\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Context\n14\t\n15\tExecutes OI-58's (c) half — minted NOW at the owner's explicit\n16\tinstruction so it is not lost to history, sequenced (needs) behind the\n17\twi448/wi483 consolidation lanes and the WI-507 doctrine so the remap\n18\treads settled ground and inherits the measured baseline.\n19\t\n20\tThe shape, grounded in the repo's proven method (the WI-467 blind\n21\tre-derivation precedent): an agent re-derives the MINIMAL module map from\n22\tthe requirements alone — blind to the live layout — with the objective\n23\tthe owner stated: serve the declared outputs while minimizing internal\n24\tsignal overlap and duplicated behavior (calls, not lines). The live map\n25\tdiffs against it; each divergence is adjudicated (consolidate / keep with\n26\treason) and filed as consolidation WIs feeding the wi448/wi483 lanes.\n27\tThe research grounding recorded on OI-58's row (minimum-description-\n28\tlength, deep-modules, the repo's own one-home findings) is the derivation\n29\tbrief's framing. Multi-session program lane; slices end green at the\n30\tcommit bar; spine-touching consolidations follow the ordinary approval\n31\tmachinery under the declared dial.\n32\t\n33\t**Orphan fold-in (owner-directed 2026-08-22):** the remap IS `SR-163`'s\n34\tverification exercise (every shipped file maps to a stakeholder outcome)\n35\t— decompose that SR into its LLR/TC as the program's slice 1 framing act,\n36\tso the blind derivation has the requirement it is checking traced before\n37\tit runs.\n38\t\n39\t### RE-VALIDATED against the amended SpecRef and the amended `SR-163`\n40\t\n41\tThe checker carried two staleness warnings on this row. Both were READ\n42\tbefore the lane opened rather than cleared by the touch, and the row\n43\tSTANDS with its scope unchanged:\n44\t\n45\t- **`SR-163` (cited).** Amended exactly once since this row was last\n46\t  touched, and the whole amendment is the addition of\n47\t  `hat_refs = [\"MAINTAINER\"]` in the perspective backfill. The normative\n48\t  `requirement`, the `rationale` and the `acceptance_criteria` cells are\n49\t  byte-identical to the text this row was minted against, so the\n50\t  obligation the program verifies has not moved. The added lens SHARPENS\n51\t  the derivation brief rather than redirecting it: `MAINTAINER` asks\n52\t  *\"can a reader two years from now tell why this exists, and what would\n53\t  break if they deleted it?\"*, which is the remap's own question asked of\n54\t  a module instead of a row.\n55\t- **`docs/requirements/open-items.toml` (the SpecRef).** `OI-58`'s own\n56\t  row has not changed since it was ruled — that commit PRECEDES this\n57\t  row's last touch, so the warning is file-level. What changed in the\n58\t  file is the arrival of `OI-60`, `OI-61`, `OI-62` and `OI-63`. All four\n59\t  were read for retasking and none touches this program's scope; they\n60\t  belong to the interface-registry lane. **`OI-63` is explicitly NOT this\n61\t  row's to execute** — it is the interface `contract` relocation question\n62\t  and is pending the owner's ruling.\n63\t\n64\t### Inherited debt, taken on at the WI-483 close\n65\t\n66\tBoth items ride along with whatever this program decomposes; neither is a\n67\tstandalone slice, and neither is discharged by the framing act.\n68\t\n69\t1. **The module-size ratchet's debt owner.** `tests/test_module_size_\n70\t   ratchet.py` names this row in its module docstring, its BASELINE\n71\t   header and its failure message, and `tests/test_import_layers.py`\n72\t   carries two more pointers. The pointer must not rot again: closing\n73\t   this row while it is named there recreates the H-05 defect the WI-483\n74\t   lane opened by fixing.\n75\t2. **M-06's four test monoliths, re-measured at that close:**\n76\t   `tests/test_integrate.py` **3,520**, `tests/test_trace.py` **2,099**,\n77\t   `tests/test_trajectory_arch.py` **1,927**, `tests/test_agent_loop.py`\n78\t   **1,640**. The standing rule is unchanged — a split RIDES ALONG with a\n79\t   subsystem decomposition and a standalone split slice is out of scope.\n80\t   The WI-483 close also banked the reason nothing noticed them growing\n81\t   5–36%: the size ratchet censuses `SCRIPTS` only, so **no armed sensor\n82\t   watches the test tree**. Whether the census should extend there is a\n83\t   real question for this program, not a drive-by.\n84\t\n85\t### Slice plan\n86\t\n87\t1. **Framing (LANDED).** Re-validate the row against the amended\n88\t   requirement, claim it, and decompose `SR-163` into its LLR/TC so the\n89\t   requirement the remap checks is traced before the derivation runs.\n90\t2. **The blind derivation.** Write the brief, run it against a strictly\n91\t   bounded input set (requirements + the depth-0 frame + the hat roster —\n92\t   never the design tier, the component or interface registries, or the\n93\t   source tree), and record brief and return durably.\n94\t3. **The alignment pass.** The only role permitted to read both sides:\n95\t   build the map — matched / present-only-in-live / present-only-in-\n96\t   derived — with each divergence adjudicated, never silently merged.\n97\t4. **File the consolidations.** One WI per adjudicated divergence that\n98\t   earns one, feeding the existing lanes rather than minting a rival\n99\t   program.\n100\t\n101\t### SLICE 1 LANDED 2026-08-25 — the framing act: `SR-163` is decomposed\n102\t\n103\t**Four rows minted, all `Drafted`, and the pair discipline is WI-510's:\n104\tname the real delivered mechanism, and state plainly what does not\n105\texist.** `SR-163` leaves the orphan list (orphans **4 → 2**; only\n106\t`SR-181` remains, owned elsewhere) with `integrity=0` unchanged.\n107\t\n108\t- **`LLR-203`** — *the shipped-file inventory and its declared\n109\t  exclusions, carrying no purpose reference.* Module\n110\t  `project-trajectory/scripts/bootstrap.py`, symbol `MAPPING`,\n111\t  `CMP-009`. Two of the parent's four finding classes are ALREADY\n112\t  delivered and driven: the scaffold-coverage walk reports a declared\n113\t  destination this repository neither carries, serves in place, nor\n114\t  declares as an absence, and reports a declared absence that has since\n115\t  materialized; the package-completeness check asks a REAL scaffold\n116\t  whether the copied helper package is the kit's module set, naming a\n117\t  missing or stale row as the cause; and the sibling-import closure\n118\t  catches a shipped script importing a file the inventory omits.\n119\t  `docs/declared-absences` is the recorded-exclusions carrier.\n120\t  **NOT DISCHARGED, on the row:** a `MAPPING` row is a source/destination\n121\t  pair plus a comment, so **no cell joins an inventoried file to a\n122\t  requirement id**; every delivered arm walks the DESTINATIONS the\n123\t  inventory declares rather than the shipped tree, so a kit file the\n124\t  inventory omits altogether is outside all of them; and the installer's\n125\t  own exclusion — the one that is load-bearing for the distribution model\n126\t  — is prose at its module rather than a row anyone can enumerate.\n127\t- **`TC-199`** — Integration / Full, verifying `SR-163` + `LLR-203`.\n128\t  Evidence is 5 EXISTING node ids across `tests/test_dogfood_sync.py`\n129\t  (the walk, its stale-entry honesty half, and the bite proof that\n130\t  removing one declared entry makes its destination reappear) and\n131\t  `tests/test_bootstrap.py` (package completeness and sibling-import\n132\t  closure, both asked of a real bootstrapped scaffold).\n133\t- **`LLR-204`** — *the purpose-reference grammar and its declared\n134\t  warn-to-gate dial, running the other direction.* Module\n135\t  `project-trajectory/scripts/gen_arch_map.py`, symbols\n136\t  `backlink_ids/scan_backlinks/read_backlink_min`, `CMP-006`. The\n137\t  `Implements:` grammar is the ONE definition of a purpose declaration in\n138\t  the source surface, and the declared threshold delivers exactly the\n139\t  warning-to-gating shape the parent's fourth clause asks for — warn at\n140\t  exit zero, gate only on the strict arm the harness appends from the\n141\t  tests rung on. **NOT DISCHARGED, two independent ways:** DIRECTION —\n142\t  the report asks whether each design row is NAMED by a source\n143\t  declaration, the parent asks the inverse, and a full reading here is\n144\t  compatible with a tree in which no file declares anything; UNIVERSE —\n145\t  the scanned roots are the declared source paths, so the grammar never\n146\t  sees a template, registry seed, launcher, workflow or process document,\n147\t  which is the greater part of the inventory.\n148\t- **`TC-200`** — Integration / Full, verifying `SR-163` + `LLR-204`.\n149\t  Evidence is 2 EXISTING node ids in `tests/test_gen_arch_map.py`: the\n150\t  grammar driven on the shared function both the map column and the\n151\t  coverage percentage read, and the warn-then-gate exit contract driven\n152\t  through the real command line on a real scaffold.\n153\t\n154\t**What this buys the derivation, which is the point of doing it first.**\n155\tThe blind agent is asked for the minimal set of modules that serves the\n156\tdeclared outputs. `SR-163` is the requirement that says every shipped\n157\tfile must be traceable to a stakeholder outcome — so the derivation's\n158\toutput IS the evidence for that row, and its two LLRs now say exactly\n159\twhich half of the join exists (the grammar and the policy) and which\n160\thalf does not (the direction and the universe). The remap is therefore\n161\tnot a free-standing opinion about layout: it is the missing side of a\n162\tjoin the registry already half-carries.\n163\t\n164\t**Deliberately NOT done here.** No purpose-coverage checker was built and\n165\tno module or symbol was invented to cite — the parent's tier discipline\n166\tis that a cited symbol must exist to be read, and the honest state is\n167\tthat the mechanism is unbuilt. Neither `SR-163` nor any other `Approved`\n168\tcell was rewritten; the four rows are authored, not amended, so no\n169\tapproval act is claimed and none was needed.\n170\t\n171\t**Watermarks** `LLR` 202 → 204, `TC` 198 → 200, via `trace.py\n172\t--bump-ids`. Record:\n173\t[../../../log.d/2026-08-25-wi508-slice1-sr163-decomposition.md](../../../log.md#2026-08-25--wi-508-slice-1-the-row-re-validated-the-lane-claimed-and--decomposed).\n174\t\n175\t### SLICE 2 LANDED 2026-08-25 — the blind derivation ran, on two axes\n176\t\n177\t**The brief was written and recorded BEFORE either agent ran**, so the question\n178\tcannot be re-written to fit the answer:\n179\t[../../../plans/2026-08-25-blind-minimal-map-brief.md](../../../plans/2026-08-25-blind-minimal-map-brief.md).\n180\tTwo agents derived the minimal module map from a **five-file input set** — the\n181\tpurpose statement, the needs, the requirements, the depth-0 frame and the hat\n182\troster — with the design tier, the component and interface registries, the\n183\tprocess masters and the source tree all held out, each for a stated reason. Two\n184\taxes, per the precedent that two teams on the SAME axis mostly agree and tell\n185\tyou little: **A worked backwards from the declared boundary outputs**, **B\n186\tclustered obligations by shared signal and failure mode**.\n187\t\n188\tReturns, verbatim and durable:\n189\t[a](../../../plans/2026-08-25-blind-derivation-a-outputs.md) (24 modules) ·\n190\t[b](../../../plans/2026-08-25-blind-derivation-b-obligations.md) (23 modules) ·\n191\tthe record, the measured agreement and the disclosures:\n192\t[../../../plans/2026-08-25-blind-minimal-map-derivation.md](../../../plans/2026-08-25-blind-minimal-map-derivation.md).\n193\t\n194\t**Agreement, measured rather than eyeballed.** Both returned complete forward\n195\tassignments (75 SRs, no id twice), so the two maps are comparable as partitions:\n196\t**97.2%** pair agreement over 2,775 SR pairs, and a best one-to-one module\n197\tcorrespondence placing **63 of 75 (84%)** identically across 22 matched module\n198\tpairs. Twelve SRs are placed differently — those are the places the requirements\n199\tunderdetermine the boundary, and they are listed in the record as INPUTS to the\n200\tadjudication rather than as findings against either map.\n201\t\n202\t**The convergence the arithmetic cannot see, and the program's biggest result so\n203\tfar.** Team A's `F5` and Team B's `M03` own **zero SRs each** and are the same\n204\tmodule: one home for the shape of a finding, its severity class, strict-mode\n205\tescalation, vacuity, and how findings compose into an exit code. Two opposite\n206\taxes independently invented it, and independently found that **no requirement\n207\tstates it** while eleven-to-thirteen rows each restate a fragment — with\n208\t`SR-158`'s own acceptance conceding the hole in the corpus's own words. That is\n209\ta missing requirement, not a layout defect, and it must NOT be filed as module\n210\twork.\n211\t\n212\t**`SR-163` split the two teams on exactly the seam slice 1 wrote.** A assigned it\n213\tto the spine-join checks, B to the package manifest — which is `LLR-204` against\n214\t`LLR-203`. Two agents that could not see the registry cut along the same line the\n215\tdecomposition did.\n216\t\n217\t**THE BLINDNESS WAS NOT TOTAL, and both teams disclosed it unprompted.** Neither\n218\tread one byte of this repository and both confined every read to the pack by\n219\tabsolute path — but the harness injected this repository's own instruction file\n220\t(and for B a memory index) into their context BEFORE the brief, naming\n221\tdirectories and several script filenames. Both checked their module names against\n222\tthat material, neither reproduced a filename as a module name, and both recorded\n223\tdeclining the obvious shortcut of using the boundary registry's script\n224\tenumeration as the module list. **The method finding: a future run must strip the\n225\tharness context, not only the input set.** It belongs to this program, not to\n226\teither team.\n227\t\n228\t**STILL OWED BY THIS ROW.** Slices 3 and 4, unchanged: the alignment pass (the\n229\tonly role permitted to read both sides, three buckets, every divergence\n230\tadjudicated with the legacy side's own rationale read FIRST), then filing the\n231\tconsolidations that earn a row. The record's §6 carries two instructions for the\n232\talignment pass — weight a live divergence by whether A and B agreed there, and\n233\tkeep the requirement-level findings out of the module-work pile.\n234\t\n235\t**Deferred to the owner: nothing new.** The derivation commissions no act; it is\n236\tone half of a diff. Record:\n237\t[../../../log.d/2026-08-25-wi508-slice2-blind-derivation.md](../../../log.md#2026-08-25--wi-508-slice-2-the-blind-derivation-runs-on-two-axes-and-both-teams-disclose-the-same-breach).\n238\t\n239\t### SLICES 3 AND 4 LANDED 2026-08-25 — the alignment, one WI filed, one question to the owner\n240\t\n241\tFull record:\n242\t[../../../plans/2026-08-25-remap-alignment.md](../../../plans/2026-08-25-remap-alignment.md).\n243\t\n244\t**The live side was read the way the registry defines it** — an LLR row's\n245\t`module` cell joined through its `sr_refs` — so `SR` → `{modules}` is a join\n246\tthat already exists and no judgement enters until the numbers are down. **75\n247\tSRs, 186 LLRs, 83 distinct modules named, and ZERO scripts named by no `Module`\n248\tcell.** Three-way pair agreement over the 71 SRs comparable on all three sides:\n249\t**A↔live 94.6%, B↔live 94.8%, A↔B 97.0%**.\n250\t\n251\t**The fact that governs every disposition below: the live map is ~3.5× finer\n252\tthan either derived map** (83 named modules against 24 and 23). A derived module\n253\tis a responsibility cluster; a live module is a file; several files realize one\n254\tcluster with no duplication provided they call a shared stage. So the question\n255\tis never \"do these live in one file\" but **\"does each home re-implement the\n256\tbehaviour, or do they all call one home for it?\"** — *calls, not lines*, applied\n257\tas a test rather than quoted.\n258\t\n259\t**THE TWELVE DISPOSITIONS: 10 keep-with-recorded-reason, 2 keep-with-the-reason-\n260\tabsent, 0 consolidate, 0 requirement gap.** That is not a shrug — the twelve are\n261\texactly the set where the two blind maps DISAGREED, so a live choice cannot be\n262\tconvicted against a derived answer that does not exist. Two of them refute a\n263\tderived map's prediction by measurement: `SR-173` (B predicted the regeneration\n264\torder would be duplicated if the seam owned it — it is stated in exactly one\n265\tplace, with its reason on `LLR-142`) and `SR-174` (B predicted non-reuse would\n266\tlive away from the mark that proves it — `intake.next_wi_id` CALLS\n267\t`trace.read_watermark` and deliberately does not catch its refusal). Two more,\n268\t`SR-043` and `SR-024`, sit at the alternative the deriving team had already\n269\tnamed and rejected in its own honesty section. The two thin ones (`LLR-024`,\n270\t`LLR-033`) carry a defensible module and no `Rationale`; both rows are\n271\t`Approved`, so writing one is an amendment over an attestation and **the\n272\towner's act, not a worker's** — banked, not fixed.\n273\t\n274\t**THE CONSOLIDATION EVIDENCE IS WHERE A AND B AGREED** (47 dispersion pairs),\n275\tand the shared-stage test dissolved most of it:\n276\t- **Declaration reading — REFUTED.** 38 modules import the shared\n277\t  `kitlib.config` stage and only `config.py` defines a declared-line reader. The\n278\t  largest apparent dispersion is one home with 38 callers.\n279\t- **Measured-value-versus-baseline — REFUSED, and the refusal matters.** Merging\n280\t  `check_perf`'s gating engine with the duplication census would put the\n281\t  disposition behind one interface and leave an owner ruling (`D-7`, which tore\n282\t  down a gated duplication step) one refactor from being undone.\n283\t- **Derived-copy freshness — REFUTED.** Team A predicted the largest saving in\n284\t  its map; each `--check` is `render() != read()` reusing the generator's own\n285\t  renderer, so what a shared module absorbs is lines, not calls.\n286\t- **Declared exception lists — UPHELD, and the rationale SHAPED it.** Five files,\n287\t  five parsers, five recorded and genuinely different grammars — a blanket merge\n288\t  would flatten five arguments. What the reading surfaced is narrower and is a\n289\t  live defect the repo diagnosed in its own words: the parse-honesty arm\n290\t  (a malformed declaring line is REPORTED, not swallowed) exists on two readers,\n291\t  is argued in `read_provenance_allow`'s docstring, was adopted by\n292\t  `_parse_kernel_allow` by explicit reference, and is **missing from three**.\n293\t\n294\t**FILED (slice 4): `WI-519`** — carry the parse-honesty arm to the three, each\n295\tkeeping its own grammar and fail-safe direction. `medium` / `ordinary`, no\n296\t`needs`: `WI-448` and `WI-483` are both closed-archived, so there is no parent\n297\tlane to feed and the row does not wait on this program.\n298\t\n299\t**DECLINED, each with its reason on the record:** the two refuted families above;\n300\tthe 48 FUSION pairs (A and B agree apart, live fuses — clustered on `agent_loop`\n301\t14, `check_trajectory` 13, `agent_common` 10, `bootstrap` 5), which restate the\n302\tmodule-size ratchet's existing debt from the requirements side and are recorded\n303\tas corroboration rather than filed as a rival program; and the census\n304\tblind-spot finding below.\n305\t\n306\t**A FINDING ABOUT THE INSTRUMENT, recorded and deliberately NOT filed.** The\n307\tstanding duplication census reads **0 / 0 / 0** on this tree while this pass\n308\tconfirmed a real repeated behaviour. No fault in the census: it hashes function\n309\tBODIES, so it measures textual duplication, and every family here is structural\n310\t— the same behaviour written differently. That is the blind derivation's\n311\tmeasurable value over the standing instrument. It is not a WI because the remedy\n312\tis not obvious and the census's own header routes changes through the owner on\n313\t`D-7`'s strength, where an over-eager duplication gate was torn down after 93%\n314\tof its findings proved to be accepted idioms.\n315\t\n316\t**TO THE OWNER: `OI-64`** — the zero-SR module both teams derived is a\n317\tREQUIREMENT gap, not a layout defect. The finding/severity/strict-escalation/\n318\tvacuity/exit-composition contract is restated in 11–13 rows and stated by none,\n319\twith `SR-158` declaring itself unsatisfied for want of a declaration surface no\n320\trow owns. Four options, recommendation (c) then (a) — measure whether the\n321\tshipped checkers honour ONE contract before minting a row that might land red.\n322\t**No module work was filed against it**, and the row says so, so a later reader\n323\tcannot mistake it for a deferred refactor.\n324\
